{"file":{"content":"# pvt_17 — actual orbits vs confined renewal words: the sole gap is realizability\n\npvt_17 gives a 10-route proof menu (top 3: convex-hull/correction-sum growth;\nrealizability large deviations; restart-density theorem) and names the single most\npromising computation: **compare actual positive-orbit confined words against synthetic\nconfined renewal controls** across A_m/3^m, restart density, least-realizing x_0, and\nstabilization cost — \"the proof will likely come from the statistic where actual orbits\ndiffer sharply from synthetic controls.\" `realizability_gap.c` runs it. The answer is\nclean and decisive: word-level statistics match; the sole sharp gap is realizability.\n\n## The experiment (`realizability_gap.c`, X=3×10⁸)\n\nActual maximal sub-equilibrium ascents (62,699) vs i.i.d. renewal words drawn from the\nempirical valuation marginal and **conditioned on the same confinement** δ_j = j log2 3\n− D_j ≥ −C (58.8% acceptance).\n\n| statistic | actual orbits | confined renewal control |\n|---|---|---|\n| restart density Pr(b=1) | 0.6684 | 0.6809 |\n| mean b | 1.470 | 1.443 |\n| A_m/3^m = (1/3)Σ 2^{−δ_j} | 7.59 | 4.65 |\n| **canonical residue log2(r_w)/D_m** | **→ 0** (pinned) | **0.99** (fills cylinder) |\n\n(Note: an *unconfined* renewal control gave A_m/3^m ≈ 1.45M — the δ-walk dips and the\ncorrection sum explodes; conditioning on confinement removes this, so A_m/3^m is O(1)\nfor both. The boundedness of A_m/3^m *is* the confinement.)\n\n## Result: no word-level statistic can witness the difference\n\nEvery functional of the valuation word alone — correction-sum growth A_m/3^m, restart\ndensity, mean valuation — **matches** between actual orbits and the confined renewal\ncontrol. The confined positive-entropy word is **symbolically indistinguishable** from a\nrenewal process. This rules out pvt_17's word-level routes:\n- **Route 1 (convex-hull / correction-sum growth):** A_m/3^m is O(1) for both, same order\n  — no growth contradiction visible at the word level.\n- **Route 3 (restart-density theorem):** densities match (0.668 vs 0.681) — a confined\n  renewal word sustains the same 3 mod 4 density, so density alone yields no contradiction\n  (consistent with pvt_8's free-Markov finding).\n- **Route 7 (block grammar):** the word is high-complexity near-product (pvt_10), and the\n  control reproduces it.","filePath":"/home/john/mynotes/collatz/docs/pvt_17_realizability_findings.md","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":95},"type":"text"}